       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg per day, which is double the usual adult maximum of 3200 mg per day. Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a meaningful risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It needs a prescriber's review before it goes into the system.\n\nAlso, medication orders should be placed by a licensed prescriber or under their direction. As CEO, you can't enter this one yourself, so please route it to the medicine team.\n\nIf the team confirms a different dose, such as 800 mg every 6 hours (3200 mg/day) or 400 mg every 6 hours, or if the intended dose is a different drug, a clinician can enter or confirm it. I can help you draft a note for the medicine team to review."
